# Q5 round-2 patch (idempotent): replaces Q5b-g, adds Q5h (HCN vs HCO+ sizes/ratio profile/forum), updates recipe/interpretation/caveats.  python3 -I build_report_q5r2.py
import json
p='/output/report.json'; r=json.load(open(p))
A=lambda n,v:{"name":n,"value":v}
old=[x for x in r['results'] if x['quantity'].startswith('Q5')]
base=[x for x in old if x['quantity'].startswith('Q5a')][0]
common=base['assumptions']
inc=[A("inclinations","N i=20-40 deg (nearly face-on), S i=70-90 deg (almost edge-on): Sakamoto+2014 (ApJ 797, 90, abstract and Sect 3); S edge-on disk PA~90 deg also in Pereira-Santaella+2024 (A&A 681, A117, Sect 1). Taken from the literature, not measured here; uniform prior in i for the Monte Carlo")]
fwd=[A("forward model","intrinsic elliptical Gaussian (or the measured m0 map as an upper-bound smear) x rotation v=vsys+Vlos,max (r.u)/sqrt(r^2+Rt^2) x sigma_int(R)=s_out+(s_c-s_out)exp(-R/0.25\"); cube convolved with the clean beam; the SAME per-pixel Gaussian fit as the data (2-px grid, r<1\"); chi2 on (v0, sigma, peak) with floors 5 km/s, 5 km/s, 10%; errors from the Jacobian x sqrt(chi2_red) x sqrt(beam-area/pixel-area)=2.7 (beam-correlated pixels)")]
inj=[A("injection","circular Gaussians of known FWHM (0-1\") convolved with the clean beam added to real line-free moment-0 noise maps (HCN 2, HCO+ 1 independent blocks; random positions >1.3\" from N, S, Bridge) and to beam-correlated noise with the off-source continuum rms (24 uJy/b); 150 realisations per cell; same fit as for the data with FWHM floor 0.1 beam (sigma>=0.01\")")]
R=[x for x in r['results'] if not x['quantity'].startswith('Q5') or x['quantity'].startswith('Q5a')]
R[[i for i,x in enumerate(R) if x['quantity'].startswith('Q5a')][0]]['value']+=" Null caveat (round 2): the shifts (1-2.5\", i.e. 4-10 beams) remove the beam-correlated signal but not the extended real structure of the shifted map, so the shifted-map null is only a test of coincidence, not of clump significance; the per-line sizes are therefore treated with the radius-dependence systematics of Q5b."
R.append({"quantity":"Q5b: deconvolved sizes of the compact dense gas at N, S (HCN 3-2, HCO+ 3-2, 1.1 mm continuum, Xb4b 0.24\"): defensible subset, ranges and upper limits (round 2, replaces the round-1 sub-clump table)","target":"N, S, clumps",
 "value":"CALIBRATION (injection-recovery, same estimator): for a single Gaussian the geometric deconvolved FWHM is recovered to +-0.01-0.03\" (95%) at the N/S HCO+ and N HCN peaks (S/N 30-80) and +-0.02-0.06\" at the weakest peak used (0.32 Jy/b km/s, S HCN) for true sizes 0.1-0.5\"; a point source returns 0.03-0.04\" with 85-93% of fits at the 0.024\" floor, so any fit below ~0.1\" (0.4 beam) is an upper limit. The noise-limited error is therefore small and the real uncertainty is the NON-GAUSSIAN structure: the real fits change by 1.1-12x between fit radii 0.3-0.6\". RULE USED: geometric FWHM kept only if no fit of the 5 radii (0.30,0.35,0.40,0.50,0.60\") is at the floor and max/min <=1.5; otherwise the range over radius is given as the constraint, floor fits are upper limits. RESULTS (geometric FWHM sqrt(maj x min), 1\"=194 pc): STABLE: N core HCO+ 0.26-0.29\" (50-56 pc; major 0.53-0.62\" x minor 0.12-0.15\" = 100-120 x 23-30 pc, i.e. a ridge, minor axis 0.5 beam); S core HCO+ 0.25-0.34\" (49-66 pc; 0.40-0.46 x 0.16-0.27\" = 78-89 x 31-52 pc); clump 1.2\" E of S, HCN 0.31-0.35\" (61-67 pc; 0.43-0.54 x 0.20-0.23\"). RANGE ONLY (not converged): N core HCN 0.20-0.47\" (39-91 pc; major 0.24-0.70\"), N-E clump HCO+ 0.32-0.52\" (62-100 pc), Bridge-E HCO+ 0.18-0.52\". UPPER LIMITS / UNCONSTRAINED (3-4 of 5 fits at the floor or size ranging 0.1-1.2\"): S core HCN (<~0.6\" = 110 pc; geo 0.09-0.57\"), N-SW HCN/HCO+, Bridge-E HCN, S-E HCO+, S-W2 HCN/HCO+. WITHDRAWN: the round-1 sizes 0.012\" and the flux-50 fit (optimiser bounds), 'N core HCN 0.72x0.31 / HCO+ 0.61x0.12' as separate sizes (see Q5h: they lie inside each other's radius range), 'HCN 1.2-1.8x larger than HCO+'. 1.1 mm continuum: S 0.21-0.26\" (marginally resolved, 40-50 pc; the same estimator returns 0.15-0.21\" for fit radii 0.3-0.6\"), S_int 3.2-3.5 mJy gives a deconvolved brightness temperature T_b=1.222e3 S/(nu^2 theta_maj theta_min)~1.5 K at 258 GHz (0.6 K peak at the beam), i.e. optically thin/low-surface-brightness dust+free-free, no compact opaque core above ~2 K; N continuum resolved 1.65x1.14\" (320x220 pc, PA 57 deg), a different shape from the dense-gas ridge (PA ~110 deg). Sizes refer to the compact (Xb4b-recovered) component (Xb4b recovers ~0.5 of the Xb4f flux).",
 "uncertainty":"stable subset: +-0.05\" (range over radius, noise term 0.01-0.03\"); others as ranges/limits","unit":"arcsec / pc","confidence":"medium",
 "evidence":"scripts/q5h_inject.py (injection), q5h2_real.py -> out/q5h/q5h_size_inj.csv, q5h_size_real.csv, q5h_size_summary.csv, q5h2.log","assumptions":common+inj})
R.append({"quantity":"Q5c: line-minus-1.1 mm continuum centroid offsets at N, S, Bridge with a null-tested budget (Xb4b, same array and phase centre; round 2)","target":"N core, S core, Bridge",
 "value":"NULL TEST (zero-offset Gaussian of 0.25\" injected into line-free noise / beam-correlated continuum noise at the real peak amplitudes, same fit, 200 realisations): 1-sigma centroid scatter per axis 2-4 mas (N,S HCO+, N HCN), 5-8 mas (S, Bridge HCN), 2 mas (S continuum 1.8 mJy/b), 7 mas (N continuum 0.55 mJy/b, S/N 23); 95% radial 5-19 mas. The thermal+beam-correlated-noise positional error is thus <=0.01\" (0.04 beam), 5-10x smaller than the round-1 Condon errors; it is NOT the limiting term. The limiting terms are (i) structure: the same estimator at fit radii 0.3/0.4/0.5/0.6\" moves the offsets by up to 0.03-0.2\", (ii) the unmeasured continuum-vs-line astrometric term (line and continuum come from one execution/phase solution, so the phase-transfer term is common and expected to be <~0.02-0.03\" ~ beam/(10 S/N) for these peaks, but cannot be separated here; Xb4d/Xb4f comparison was not repeated, no independent continuum image exists). MEASURED (east, north; arcsec; range over radius 0.3-0.6\"): S HCO+-cont (-0.007..-0.001, -0.049..-0.028) = 0.03-0.05\" (6-10 pc, 0.12-0.2 beam), stable in sign, 10-20x the null scatter, i.e. a real small displacement of the HCO+ centroid south of the continuum OR a structure/beam-shape systematic of that size; S HCN-cont unconstrained (0.04-0.26\", HCN fit at the floor); N core HCO+-cont (+0.069..+0.096, -0.025..+0.012) = 0.07-0.10\" (14-19 pc, 0.3-0.4 beam), stable (HCO+ peak east of the continuum); N core HCN-cont (-0.019..+0.036, -0.009..+0.021) = 0.01-0.04\" (consistent with zero, <=8 pc); hence HCN-HCO+ peak displacement at N 0.05-0.09\" (HCN west; at matched 0.30\" beam 0.047\"; 10-17 pc, 0.2-0.35 beam). Bridge: continuum 0.14-0.18 mJy/b and extended (FWHM 0.9-1.0\"), line offsets 0.1-0.7\" depend on radius: not defined. LIMITS to quote: line and 1.1 mm centroids coincide to <=0.10\" (<=20 pc, <=0.4 beam) at N and <=0.05\" (<=10 pc, <=0.2 beam) at S (HCO+); the round-1 criterion of p0001 (<=0.13 beam = 0.03\") is NOT demonstrated at N or S (S HCO+ 0.12-0.2 beam). Team-b's 'HCN/HCO+ peaks coincide with continuum to <=0.07\"' (p0005) is consistent at S and for N HCN; for N HCO+ we find up to 0.10\".",
 "uncertainty":"statistical (null) <=0.01\"; systematic (radius/structure) 0.03-0.1\"","unit":"arcsec / pc / beam","confidence":"medium",
 "evidence":"scripts/q5h2_real.py -> out/q5h/q5h_offsets.csv, q5h_offset_null.csv, q5h2.log","assumptions":common+inj})
R.append({"quantity":"Q5d: velocity fields, gradients and a beam-convolved rotation model at N and S (per-pixel Gaussian fits plus forward model, HCN and HCO+ 3-2, native 0.25\")","target":"N, S, Bridge",
 "value":"DATA (planar gradient of per-pixel v0, km/s per arcsec, HCN / HCO+; error includes beam-correlation inflation): N R<0.4\": 182+-22 / 191+-26 (PA of increasing velocity 96/95 deg); R<0.6\": 133+-13 / 134+-13 (85/85); R<0.8\": 106+-7 / 107+-7 (79/79); R<1\": 87+-5 / 84+-5 (78/77); R<1.4\": 64+-4 / 59+-3 (76/76); R<2\": 57+-6 / 46+-2 (66/69): well measured, residual rms 13-17 km/s at R<=1\", axis swing 96->66 deg agrees with Sakamoto+2014. S: R<0.4\": 69+-59 / 129+-57 (1.2 / 2.3 sigma); R<0.6\": 138+-43 / 140+-28; R<0.8\": 138+-28 / 113+-17; R<1.0\": 112+-36 / 96+-12; R<1.4\": 92+-36 / 69+-9; R<2\": 36+-18 / 45+-6 at PA 100-144 deg (E-W, as the edge-on disk of Sakamoto+2014). The residual rms about the plane (31-40 km/s at R<=0.8\", 82-106 at R>=1\") is as large as the signal for S: S is not a clean rotator, and the gradient at R<0.4\" is UNCONSTRAINED (HCN consistent with 0). The round-1 statement 'steepest gradient 0.5\" east of the nucleus' is withdrawn (no error was given; the per-radius planar gradients carry no information on where along the axis the gradient is steepest). Bridge 38+-8 / 36+-9 km/s/\" N-S at R<0.6\". FORWARD MODEL (beam-convolved cube, same pixel fits, jointly v, sigma and peak; two intensity assumptions give the same numbers within the errors): N HCO+ / HCN: kinematic PA 80+-2 / 80+-2 deg, Vlos,max = 64.7+-2.1 / 65.5+-2.5 km/s, turnover radius Rt=0.04+-0.08 / 0.07+-0.07\" (<=0.2\", the curve is flat already at R>=0.25\" = 50 pc), vsys 2776 / 2774 km/s, chi2_red 3.4 (residuals 1.1-2.4 sigma units); S HCO+: PA 110+-4 deg, Vlos,max 78+-5 km/s, Rt=0.03+-0.16\" (inner rise unconstrained), vsys 2794+-4, chi2_red 13.6 (residual 4 sigma units: poor); S HCN fails (chi2_red 69, PA 143+-11 deg, vsys 2816 km/s): the HCN S gas is not described by this rotator, so S rotation is taken from HCO+ only and only as an order-of-magnitude model. The S systemic velocity 2794 differs from the peak-pixel centroid (2710-2740) by 60-80 km/s. These are projected values; deprojection uses i from the literature (Q5f).",
 "uncertainty":"N: gradient 3-12% (R>=0.6\"), model Vlos +-3 km/s; S: 30-100% at R<=0.8\", model +-5 km/s statistical, factor ~2 systematic","unit":"km/s per arcsec; km/s; deg","confidence":"medium",
 "evidence":"scripts/q5e_kin.py -> out/q5/q5e_grad.csv; scripts/q5i_kinfit.py -> out/q5h/q5i_{gauss,map}_{N,S}.log and json","assumptions":common+fwd})
R.append({"quantity":"Q5e: line widths at native resolution (peak pixel, one beam, and larger apertures) and intrinsic sigma(R) from the beam-convolved model","target":"N, S, Bridge",
 "value":"OBSERVED (single Gaussian, baseline-subtracted spectrum, peak pixel of Xb4b 0.25\"): sigma (FWHM km/s), HCN / HCO+: N 70.4+-0.9 (165.8) / 55.7+-0.8 (131.1); S 49.6+-1.4 (116.9) / 48.9+-0.7 (115.1); Bridge 33.4+-1.2 (78.8) / 38.3+-0.8 (90.2); beam-sized aperture r=0.12\": N 61.8/56.1, S 46.1/46.5; r=1\": N 71/67, S 89/90 (S mixes E-W rotation and the outflow base). Mean per-pixel sigma at r<0.2\" 59.7 (HCN), 54.6 (HCO+) at N and 53.0 (HCO+) at S, falling to 25-37 at r=0.7-1.0\". BEAM SMEARING from the forward model (noise-free model with sigma_int~0, same per-pixel fit): pure-rotation smear sigma at r<0.2 / 0.2-0.4 / 0.4-0.7 / 0.7-1.0\" = 24-25 / 14 / 8 / 5 km/s at N (HCO+, HCN), 16 / 17 / 9 / 4 km/s at S (HCO+). The round-1 value 13.5 km/s (planar-gradient estimate) underestimates the central smear by ~2x, but because it adds in quadrature it changed sigma by only 10-15% at the peak (N HCN 70 -> 66 km/s). INTRINSIC sigma(R) (model, median and 68% interval, errors inflated for beam-correlated pixels), HCO+ / HCN at N: R=0: 63 [56,71] / 79 [72,88]; 0.12\": 48 [43,52] / 58 [54,63]; 0.25\": 38 [35,40] / 44 [41,47]; 0.5\": 28 [27,30] / 31 [30,32]; 1\": 24 [23,25] / 24 [23,26] km/s (centrally peaked, ~R^-0.5 inside 0.5\", flat ~24 km/s outside: the N sigma peak is intrinsic, 55-65% of the observed peak-pixel dispersion, not beam smearing); S HCO+: 63 [41,81] at R=0, 52 [39,64] at 0.12\", 45 [37,52] at 0.25\", 38 [35,41] at 0.5\", 35 [31,38] km/s at 1\" (S HCN: not fitted reliably). One-beam intrinsic sigma (observed peak-pixel minus the model smear in quadrature): N HCN 66, HCO+ 50, S HCO+ ~47-50 km/s (+-5). HCN/HCO+ intrinsic sigma ratio at N 1.1-1.25 at R<=0.25\" (about 1-2 sigma of the inflated errors), 1.0 at R>=0.75\"; consistent with team-b p0007 (FWHM ratio 1.085+-0.015, core value within 1 sigma of the aperture null, no saturation broadening). Peak spectra are not purely Gaussian (half-maximum widths agree with Gaussian FWHM to 10%). The widths are 2-3x the cloud dispersions of Brunetti+2022 (CO 2-1, median 23 km/s at 90 pc) and within the nuclear range of Brunetti+2021 (10-200 km/s at 55-120 pc); Brunetti+2024 attribute the high nuclear dispersions partly to outflow/jet contamination.",
 "uncertainty":"observed +-1-3 km/s; intrinsic +-4-10 km/s (model, inflated), S +-10-20 km/s at R<0.25\"","unit":"km/s","confidence":"medium",
 "evidence":"scripts/q5e_kin.py -> out/q5/q5e_width.csv; scripts/q5i_kinfit.py -> out/q5h/q5i_*.log","assumptions":common+fwd})
R.append({"quantity":"Q5f: dynamical and virial masses of the N and S nuclear disks from the beam-convolved rotation model (inclination Monte Carlo), Mdyn(N)/Mdyn(S) (round 2)","target":"N, S",
 "value":"Mdyn(<R)=Vc^2 R/G with Vc=Vlos(R)/sin i, i uniform N 20-40 deg, S 70-90 deg (median and 16-84%): N (HCO+ model; HCN within 3%): R=48 pc (0.25\") 1.7 (1.2-2.8)e8; 97 pc 3.7 (2.6-6.0)e8; 194 pc 7.6 (5.3-12)e8 Msun [with an isotropic pressure term Vc^2+3 sigma_int^2: 2.3 (1.7-3.3), 4.3 (3.1-6.6), 8.3 (6.0-13)e8]. S (HCO+ model only; HCN not usable): 48 pc 0.58 (0.41-0.78)e8; 97 pc 1.3 (1.1-1.5)e8; 194 pc 2.8 (2.5-3.2)e8 [with pressure term 1.3, 2.3, 4.5e8]. The S intervals are inclination only; the S model has chi2_red 13.6 and an unconstrained inner rise, so add a factor ~2 systematic (97 pc: 0.7-2.6e8). Mdyn(N)/Mdyn(S) at 97 pc = 2.8 (rotation only) or 1.9 (with pressure), range 1.4-5 allowing for the inclination and factor-2 S systematics; the round-1 value 4.0 (2.3-10) is replaced. This is consistent with ~2.5+-1 at 1 kpc diameter from Sakamoto+2014 (CO 3-2 line widths). N masses agree with round 1 (3.4e8 at 97 pc, 5.5e8 at 194 pc) and with the R-dependence of Sakamoto+2014; the S mass at 194 pc is 2x the round-1 value because the model holds the curve flat to R=1\" while the symmetric-bin curve fell (mixing with the outflow base): treat S(194 pc) as an upper estimate. VIRIAL with the beam-corrected one-beam sigma (Q5e) and the stable sizes (Q5b): M=1040 sigma^2 R_pc, R=1.91 sigma_r: N core HCO+ sigma 50 km/s, R=1.91 x (0.29\"/2.355 x 194)=46 pc -> 1.2e8; N core HCN sigma 54-66, R=38-74 pc (size range) -> (1.2-3.5)e8; S core HCO+ sigma 47-50, R=39-53 pc -> (1.0-1.4)e8 Msun. Mvir/Mdyn(<48 pc, with pressure term) = 0.5-1.5 at N and 0.8-1.1 at S: virial and rotation masses agree, i.e. the compact dense gas is gravitationally bound in the nuclear disks and its widths are not outflow broadening. Crossing time R/sigma: N 0.9-1.5 Myr, S 1.0-1.5 Myr. Dynamical mass includes stars and any other gas; N mass scales as 1/sin^2 i (x2.1 at i=20 deg, x0.6 at 40 deg).",
 "uncertainty":"N M(<97 pc) 3.7e8 (x0.7..x1.6 for i 40-20 deg); S 1.3e8 (factor 2); ratio N/S 1.4-5","unit":"Msun","confidence":"low",
 "evidence":"scripts/q5i_kinfit.py, q5k_mdyn.py -> out/q5h/q5k.log, q5i_*.json; scripts/q5g_summary.py -> out/q5/q5g_virial.csv (round-1 virial)","assumptions":common+inc+fwd+[A("virial","M=1040 sigma_los^2 R_pc with R=1.91 sigma_r (Rosolowsky & Leroy 2006); sigma = observed peak-pixel dispersion with the forward-model smear subtracted in quadrature")]})
R.append({"quantity":"Q5h: HCN vs HCO+ size of the N and S cores at matched resolution, the HCN/HCO+ ratio profile, and reconciliation with team-b p0005/p0007 and team-a p0005-r02","target":"N core, S core",
 "value":"Gaussian-fit sizes cannot separate the two lines: N core HCN 0.20-0.47\" (major 0.24-0.70\") vs HCO+ 0.26-0.29\" (major 0.53-0.62\", minor 0.12-0.15\") over fit radii 0.3-0.6\": the ranges overlap, so the round-1 'HCN 0.72x0.31 vs HCO+ 0.61x0.12 at N' is not a >3 sigma size difference (the noise-only injection error is 0.01-0.03\", the radius/model systematics are 0.1-0.25\"); S core HCN is unconstrained (<~0.6\"). MODEL-INDEPENDENT test (both cubes' +-350 km/s moment-0 maps convolved to a common 0.30\" circular beam, profiles about the HCO+ peak, background from r=1.5-2\" or 1-1.5\" or none): half-light radius r50(HCN)-r50(HCO+) = -0.06 (N; -0.01..-0.06 over the background choice) and -0.07 (S; -0.04..-0.08) arcsec, noise sd 0.002-0.010\"; r50 N 0.50 vs 0.56\" (97 vs 109 pc), S 0.37 vs 0.44\" (72 vs 86 pc); r75 N 0.69 vs 0.75\", S 0.59 vs 0.69\". So HCN is equal to or up to ~15% MORE COMPACT than HCO+ at both nuclei (HCN/HCO+ r50 ratio 0.89-0.98 N, 0.85-0.90 S); the round-1 statement 'HCN is 1.2-1.8x larger than HCO+' is withdrawn (it came from unstable single-Gaussian fits of HCN at larger fit radii). HCN/HCO+ moment-0 ratio profile at 0.30\" (annuli 0-0.1/0.1-0.2/0.2-0.3/0.3-0.45/0.45-0.6/0.6-0.8/0.8-1.0/1.0-1.5\"): N 1.01/0.99/0.97/0.93/0.80/0.73/0.67/0.37 (+-0.01-0.015); S 0.37/0.35/0.37/0.40/0.26/0.24/0.26/0.19 (+-0.01-0.02). RECONCILIATION: (i) agrees with team-b p0005 (N 0.97/0.87/0.65/0.41 for <0.25/0.25-0.5/0.5-1/1-2\" at 0.25\") and team-a p0005-r02 (0.98/0.95/0.87/0.64/0.45 at 0.30\"): the N core has ratio ~1.0 inside r~0.3\" (<=60 pc) and falls to 0.4 by 1-1.5\"; this is a radial profile difference (HCN falls faster outward than HCO+), not a larger HCN size; r02's 'resolved ~0.6\" (FWHM) excess' is the 0.3-0.6\" shoulder of this profile. (ii) S is flat at 0.35-0.40 inside 0.45\" and drops to ~0.25 outside (p0005: flat 0.37-0.43 to 3\" at 0.94\"/blended beams; consistent at 0.25\" inside 0.45\", slightly lower beyond). (iii) p0007's width null (HCN/HCO+ FWHM 1.085+-0.015 in 0.30\" r<0.25\") is consistent with equal-size, equal-width cores and our intrinsic sigma ratio 1.1-1.25 at R<=0.25\" (1-2 sigma). Consequence for Q1/Q2 beam filling: a common filling factor for HCN and HCO+ (equal within ~15%, HCN not larger) is supported at the N and S cores at 0.25-0.3\" resolution; the ratio gradient is carried by the excitation/opacity/abundance profile, not by different filling. At the S core the HCN/HCO+ ratio of 0.37 at equal size means the S deficit is in brightness temperature, not geometric dilution.",
 "uncertainty":"r50 differences +-0.01\" (noise), +-0.03\" (background choice); ratio +-0.01-0.02 per annulus","unit":"arcsec / ratio","confidence":"medium",
 "evidence":"scripts/q5j_ratio_size.py -> out/q5h/q5j.log, q5j_profiles.csv; q5h_size_summary.csv","assumptions":common+[A("matching","both maps convolved to 0.30\" circular (native beams 0.246x0.237 / 0.246x0.232\" PA -49); +-350 km/s window; errors from 2/1 line-free blocks, 200 rolled realisations")]})
R.append({"quantity":"Q5g: SUMMARY (round 2) - sizes, offsets, kinematics and what is not supported at 0.24\"; inputs for Q1, Q2, Q16","target":"N, S",
 "value":"(1) Sizes: only the N-core HCO+ (0.26-0.29\", 50-56 pc; a ridge 100-120 x 23-30 pc), S-core HCO+ (0.25-0.34\", 49-66 pc) and a clump 1.2\" E of S in HCN (0.31-0.35\") have stable deconvolved sizes (<= 1.5 beam, geometric FWHM); N-core HCN is 0.20-0.47\" (range), everything else is an upper limit or unconstrained. The injection test shows a noise-limited size error of 0.01-0.06\"; the radius-dependence of the real (non-Gaussian) structure is the true error. (2) HCN is not larger than HCO+: matched-beam half-light radii are 0.50 vs 0.56\" (N) and 0.37 vs 0.44\" (S); ratio ~1.0 inside r~0.3\" at N, 0.37 flat at S; common filling is supported (round-1 'HCN 1.2-1.8x larger' withdrawn). (3) Offsets: lines and 1.1 mm continuum coincide to <=0.10\" (20 pc, 0.4 beam) at N and <=0.05\" (10 pc, 0.2 beam) at S; thermal positional errors are <=0.01\"; measured displacements (S HCO+ 0.03-0.05\" S of the continuum; N HCO+ 0.07-0.10\" E; N HCN-HCO+ peaks 0.05-0.09\") are 0.1-0.4 beam, inseparable from structure/astrometric systematics; Bridge undefined. (4) Kinematics: N is a flat rotation curve (Vlos 65+-3 km/s, kinematic PA 80+-2 deg, Rt<=0.2\"), S is only roughly described by an E-W rotator (HCO+: PA 110+-4 deg, Vlos 78+-5; chi2_red 13.6; HCN not fitted) and its gradient at R<0.4\" is unconstrained (69+-59 km/s/\" in HCN, 1.2 sigma). (5) Beam smearing explains 24-25 of the 55-70 km/s peak-pixel dispersion at N and ~16 of ~50 at S; intrinsic sigma is centrally peaked at N (63-79 at R~0 to 24 km/s at 1\"); one-beam intrinsic sigma N 50 (HCO+) - 66 (HCN), S 47-50 km/s. (6) Masses: Mdyn(N, <97 pc) 3.7 (2.6-6.0)e8, Mdyn(S, <97 pc) 1.3e8 (factor 2), N/S 1.4-5 (2.8 rotation only, 1.9 with pressure); virial masses 1.0-3.5e8 at R 40-75 pc agree with the rotation masses (0.5-1.5): the dense gas is bound, not outflow-broadened. (7) Not supported: '>=5 N sub-clumps', single-Gaussian N sizes, S continuum below ~40 pc, an S rotation law inside 0.4\", 'steepest gradient 0.5\" E of S'. Needed: CO 3-2/2-1 or HCN 1-0 at <=0.3\" (not in the archive) for sigma(R) and mass-to-light independent masses; visibilities for uv-plane fits.",
 "uncertainty":"see Q5b-h","unit":None,"confidence":"medium",
 "evidence":"Q5a-h; out/q5/ and out/q5h/ logs; scripts/q5*.py","assumptions":common})
r['results']=R
