r['interpretation']=s[:a]+"[Q5 round 2] At 0.24\" the N nucleus is a ~50 pc (HCO+ 0.26-0.29\" geometric FWHM) dense core on a 100x25 pc ridge with a flat rotation curve (Vlos 65+-3 km/s, i.e. ~130 km/s deprojected at i=30 deg; Mdyn(<97 pc) ~4e8 Msun, factor 0.7-1.6 from the inclination) and a centrally peaked intrinsic dispersion (63-79 km/s at R~0 to 24 km/s at 1\"), of which beam smearing is 24-25 km/s of the observed 55-70; the S nucleus is a similar-size (0.25-0.34\") HCO+ core in an E-W disk that is only roughly rotating (PA 110+-4 deg, Vlos 78+-5 km/s, chi2_red 14; Mdyn(<97 pc) ~1e8 within a factor 2; no usable gradient at R<0.4\"). Virial and rotation masses agree, so the dense-gas widths are gravitational, not outflow broadening. HCN is not more extended than HCO+: at matched 0.30\" resolution r50 is 0.50 vs 0.56\" (N) and 0.37 vs 0.44\" (S), the HCN/HCO+ ratio is ~1.0 within 0.3\" at N and falls to 0.4 at 1-1.5\" (agrees with team-b p0005 and team-a p0005-r02), and flat 0.37 at S; the round-1 HCN-larger-than-HCO+ result is withdrawn and a common filling factor is supported to ~15%. Line and 1.1 mm centroids coincide to <=0.1\" (N) and <=0.05\" (S) (<0.4 beam), thermal position errors <=0.01\"; Gaussian sizes below ~0.1\" and all sub-clump fits other than N-core HCO+, S-core HCO+ and the S-E HCN clump are unconstrained."
cav="Q5 (round 2): (a) Xb4b recovers ~0.5 of the flux, so sizes are of the compact component; (b) injection calibrates the noise-limited error (0.01-0.06\") only: the dominant error is non-Gaussian structure (radius dependence 1.1-12x), so sizes beyond the stable subset are ranges/limits; the null maps are only 2 (HCN) and 1 (HCO+) independent blocks, reused at random positions; (c) the offset budget has no independent astrometric check (one execution, one continuum image, no repeat in Xb4d/Xb4f), so 0.03-0.1\" displacements are limits, not detections; (d) the forward model assumes an axisymmetric thin disk with a single Gaussian (or measured-map) intensity, one kinematic axis, no warp/outflow, sigma_int(R) with an exponential form; N fit chi2_red 3.4, S 13.6 (HCN S 69, not used); errors are inflated by the pixel-correlation factor 2.7 but are not full posteriors; the N-S Mdyn ratio of 1.4-5 reflects inclination priors (N 20-40, S 70-90 deg, from Sakamoto+2014) and the poor S fit; (e) the HCN/HCO+ half-light-radius comparison is a model-independent result at 0.30\" but depends on the background annulus (0.01-0.03\"); (f) clean beam is Gaussianised (the Xb4b PSF has side lobes), which can bias deconvolved sizes <~0.05\"; (g) dynamical masses include stars and all gas; virial masses assume virialised gas."
